From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:13:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] thunderbolt: apple: offer the attached-dock sleep
 owner on the J604 too

With thunderbolt.cio_s2r set, the T8132 CIO sleep owner puts the host
router to sleep before a deep system sleep and restores the CIO PHY,
the NHI's DART and the controller after the firmware wake. Without it a
deep sleep with a dock or a Thunderbolt display attached takes the
stock path, which was never written for a wake that took the block's
power. The owner was offered on the J713 only.

The J604 has three ports on the same T8132 ACIO. The owner binds per
NHI, to its own ACIO's "cio" PHY and to the DART in its own iommus
property, so the port count does not matter. Offer it on the J604 as
well. cio_s2r stays off by default, so nothing changes until it is set
on the command line for a docked sleep test.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/thunderbolt/apple-cio-sleep.c | 6 +++++-
 drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c           | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/apple-cio-sleep.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/apple-cio-sleep.c
index 6a75dbf6b8..1cb4e37950 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/apple-cio-sleep.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/apple-cio-sleep.c
@@ -103,8 +103,12 @@ static int apple_nhi_cio_bind(struct apple_nhi *anhi)
 
 	if (!cio_s2r)
 		return 0;
+	/*
+	 * The J713 and the J604 (three ports, the same T8132 ACIO): each NHI binds its own ACIO's
+	 * CIO PHY and its own DART, so nothing here depends on the port count.
+	 */
 	if (anhi->acio->hw != &apple_cio_t8132_hw ||
-	    !of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j713"))
+	    !(of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j713") || of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j604")))
 		return 0;
 	ret = apple_nhi_cio_bind_owner(anhi);
 	if (ret == -EPROBE_DEFER)
diff --git a/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c b/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
index 587754abb9..e90e22c3b6 100644
--- a/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
+++ b/drivers/thunderbolt/apple.c
@@ -336,7 +336,7 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(dpin_mode_value,
 
 static bool cio_s2r;
 module_param(cio_s2r, bool, 0400);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(cio_s2r, "Enable experimental J713 attached-dock system sleep");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(cio_s2r, "Enable experimental J713/J604 attached-dock system sleep");
 
 struct apple_dpin_binding;
 
